.SH TOKEN FORMAT
The authentication token is 32 bytes of entropy read from
\f[CR]/dev/urandom\f[R], hex\-encoded to a 64\-character string.
The raw bytes are zeroed after encoding.
The token file is written with 0600 permissions.
.SH DLL ARCHITECTURE
.IP
.EX
bash.exe \-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-+
                    +\-\-> cygbash\-5.1.dll \-\-> cygwin1.dll
bash\-server.exe \-\-\-+                    \-\-> KERNEL32.dll
.EE
.PP
Both executables share the same Bash interpreter DLL.
\f[CR]bashclient.exe\f[R] is standalone and does not link against
\f[CR]cygbash\-5.1.dll\f[R].
